  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A theurge does not receive his divine spells directly from the deity or other mystical force he venerates. Instead, he must search for and collect new divine spells to record in his prayer book, much the same as he does with arcane spells for his spellbook. These divine spells can come from divine scrolls, holy tablets, or other magical writings. A theurge cannot prepare any divine spell not recorded in his prayer book. A theurge begins play with a prayer book containing all 0-level cleric spells plus three 1st-level cleric spells of the player’s choice.</p>\n<p>The theurge may also select a number of additional 1st-level cleric spells equal to his Wisdom modifier to add to his prayer book. At each new theurge level, he gains two new cleric spells of any spell level or levels that he can cast (based on his new theurge level). At any time, a theurge can also add divine spells found on scrolls or in other magical writings to his prayer book.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/theurge#toc5\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
